- op: discuss  # 45d5
  at: '2026-08-13T09:41:37Z'  # 45d5
  by: agent  # 45d5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 45d5
  clock: 5  # 45d5
  nonce: 45d5  # 45d5
  message: "REMEDIES (b) AND (c) LANDED TOGETHER. Item moves to satisfied; the residual it\nwas still open on -- \"rc 0 is IDENTICAL whether or not a repo-supplied entry is\nload-bearing\" -- no longer reproduces.\n\nWHY BOTH, RATHER THAN (b) ALONE. (b) is a distinct exit code and (c) is\nADR-0016 section 4's fourth verdict. Shipping (b) by itself would have put the\nfact in the exit code while the JSON envelope still said \"confirmed\" -- two\nsurfaces disagreeing about one run, which is the drift this repo keeps paying\nfor. One concept, three surfaces (value, envelope, rc), derived once.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-run on the working tree with all three arms in one\nsession. Fixture is this item's own repro: an 11-line file whose whole body is\nos.remove(launder(os.environ[\"API_KEY\"])) with launder returning its argument.\n\n  1. THE FILED CASE -- the lie shipped IN-TREE as a dotfile and referenced from\n     the repo's own claims-file extra_catalogs: block, no flag passed by\n     whoever runs the tool:\n       BEFORE  Verdict: confirmed              rc 0\n       AFTER   Verdict: confirmed_with_caveats rc 3\n       \"CAVEAT (user_supplied_sanitizer): A sanitizer supplied by the analysed\n        repository is credited with removing 1 flow(s) that would otherwise\n        have been reported: app.launder. The tool cannot check that the named\n        function neutralises the taint; it takes the repository's word for it.\"\n\n  2. NON-DESTRUCTION -- same fixture, no sanitizer file: violated rc 1, before\n     and after. The finding is still MADE; only what happens to a clean verdict\n     changed.\n\n  3. rc 0 STILL EXISTS -- a fixture with no flow at all: confirmed rc 0. The\n     caveat is not raised on every verdict, which is the property that keeps it\n     worth reading.\n\nTHE DISCRIMINATOR IS PINNED BY UNIT TEST, NOT BY THE LIVE PROBE, and that limit\nis stated rather than papered over. The sharper live arm -- a SHIPPED sanitizer\nholding a verdict up, which must stay plain `confirmed` rc 0 -- could not be\nbuilt: every shipped python sanitizer is a cryptography.fernet method, and that\nmodule is uncatalogued for io_primitives, so the coverage gate caps the run at\nrc 2 for a reason unrelated to what is being measured (the same confound that\nate an earlier probe on this item). Declaring cryptography.fernet in an overlay\nwould require asserting an I/O boundary that is not true of it, which would\nmake the measurement rest on a false row -- so the built-in arm is covered by\ntest_a_built_in_sanitizer_still_earns_a_plain_confirmed and\ntest_prose_and_verdict_value_cannot_disagree instead.\n\nSTRUCTURE, because a fourth enum value is the change that punches holes in\nscattered literals. CONFIRMING_VERDICTS is the single membership test and\n_require_coverage_to_confirm consumes it: had that gate kept `!= \"confirmed\"`,\na BLIND analysis would have returned confirmed_with_caveats instead of\ninconclusive, widening the false-confirm class INV-bitig and INV-javam closed.\ntest_blindness_still_dominates_a_caveated_verdict pins that direction.\n_credited_sanitizers is the one home for \"which sanitizers were credited, and\nwhose\" -- the prose clause and the caveat are two consumers of one fact, and\ntest_prose_and_verdict_value_cannot_disagree asserts they move together in BOTH\ndirections over three finding populations.\n\nEvery reader of `verdict` was enumerated BEFORE the value was added: the\ncoverage gate, the CLI icon/summary/exit-code block, and\nscripts/generate-security-md -- whose _BADGE dict returns \"\" for an unknown\nverdict, so a caveated claim would have rendered indistinguishable from a\nconfirmed one in the document whose entire purpose is not overstating what was\nverified.\n\nTHE \"NOT SWEPT\" QUESTION ON THIS ITEM IS NOW ANSWERED, AND THE ANSWER IS YES.\nWhether user-supplied SOURCES or SINKS can suppress a finding by the same\nroute: they can, by a DIFFERENT mechanism. Sanitizers .extend() the catalogue;\nsources and sinks merge through _merge_with_user_override, where a user entry\nmatching a shipped one on (module, name, kind) REPLACES it. A user sink\nre-declaring pathlib.Path / write_text out of the host_fs zone takes a real\nviolated rc 1 to confirmed rc 0 -- by the --taint-sinks flag AND the in-tree\nextra_catalogs: route -- with caveats: [] and no disclosure on the verdict.\nFiled as INV-faput. It is NOT covered here and cannot be by this mechanism:\nthe shipped sink leaves the catalogue before propagation runs, so no flow is\nconstructed and there is no finding to attribute. The scope limit is written\ninto the CAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER docstring so a later reader cannot take\nthis for the class.\n\nThe first run of that sweep was a FALSE NULL and is recorded because it nearly\nshipped as \"sinks cannot suppress\": the probe spelled the user row\n`module: pathlib, methods: [Path.write_text]` while the shipped entry is\n`module='pathlib.Path', name='write_text'`, so the override key never matched.\nCaught by reading the MERGED CATALOGUE rather than the verdict.\n\nCONSUMER CONTRACT, stated plainly because this is the part that can bite:\na gate written `verify-claims ... || exit 1` now FAILS on rc 3 where it passed.\nThat is deliberate and fail-closed, and it applies to hypergumbo's own\nself-proof, which declares a zone-barrier sanitizer through extra_catalogs: by\ndesign. No exemption was carved for it -- \"except our own\" is the dishonesty\nthis item exists to close. The self-proof reports 18/18 inconclusive today\n(INV-dabuf), so no verdict there moves yet; when INV-dabuf's bash residual is\nclosed, expect the self-proof to land on rc 3 rather than rc 0.\n\nRE-RUN ON THE MERGED TREE (74789a3a47), all three arms, per closure-evidence\ndiscipline -- the pre-merge run is not what closes this:\n    lie (in-tree extra_catalogs:)  rc=3  Verdict: confirmed_with_caveats\n    baseline (no sanitizer file)   rc=1  Verdict: violated\n    clean (no flow at all)         rc=0  Verdict: confirmed\nplus the CAVEAT line rendered on the text surface naming app.launder."  # 45d5
- op: discuss  # c058
  at: '2026-08-13T22:20:08Z'  # c058
  by: agent  # c058
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c058
  clock: 6  # c058
  nonce: c058  # c058
  message: "SECOND CAVEAT KIND LANDED on this item's machinery (dev 60ba704378): opaque_boundary, ADR-0016 section 4's original specified consumer, owner-authorized. The kind axis this item shipped took it without change, which is the property it was designed for. One defect surfaced by the extension and fixed: the taint arm's append was unguarded, so a claims file holding both claim kinds recorded opaque_boundary TWICE on the boundary verdict -- caveats is a surface consumers COUNT. _merge_caveat now folds by kind and keeps the union of entries. Recorded here because it is the mirror of INV-virat: assign->append stops erasure and invites duplication."  # c058
